ckage-lock.json); lines 8–12: `build`/`test`/`lint` scripts are exactly `turbo run build` / `turbo run test` / `turbo run lint`. PASS\n3. Files committed in `6cc5d66`, tracked by git, clean status; tests execute with exit 0. PASS\n\n**Observations (below reportable threshold, noted only for completeness):**\n- `\"packageManager\": \"npm@10\"` omits a patch version (corepack prefers a full version like `npm@10.8.2`). The story's AC explicitly requires `npm@10`, so this is spec-compliant — not a defect.\n- Test \"AC 2\" label bundles the npm pin and engines assertions; the AC numbering in tests doesn't map 1:1 to the story's three criteria, but every acceptance criterion is covered by at least one assertion.\n- `assert.equal` (loose) vs `assert.strictEqual` in a `node:assert/strict` file — the file imports `node:assert/strict`, so `equal` is strict anyway. No issue.\n\nNo security, quality, or correctness issues found. The diff is a minimal, well-tested scaffold that exactly matches the story spec.\n\n## Review Summary\n\n| Severity | Count | Status |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| CRITICAL | 0     | pass   |\n| HIGH     | 0     | pass   |\n| MEDIUM   | 0     | info   |\n| LOW      | 0     | note   |\n\nVerdict: APPROVE","output":"\n\nAll checks complete. Both files match the committed version, tests pass, and the working tree is clean for the in-scope paths.\n\n## Review Findings\n\n**Verification performed:**\n- `git show 6cc5d66` — commit adds `package.json`, `test/package.test.cjs`, `package-lock.json`, and a `node_modules/` gitignore entry. Working-tree `package.json` and `test/package.test.cjs` are identical to the committed versions.\n- `node --test test/package.test.cjs` — 4 tests, 4 pass, 0 fail, exit 0.\n- `git ls-files package.json test/package.test.cjs` — both tracked; `git status --porcelain -- package.json test/` — clean.\n\n**Acceptance criteria check:**\n1. `package.json` (line 2–6): `name: \"nextmove\"`, `private: true`, `workspaces: [\"apps/*\"]`,